+## Start an Agent in a new session
+
+To start one supported interactive Agent in the first pane of every new persistent session, opt in with its `herdr agent start --kind` label:
+
+```toml
+[session]
+auto_start_agent = "opencode"
+```
+
+The setting is unset by default. It runs only when a session has no saved state. It does not run again for a restored session, client attach, config reload, live handoff, or `--no-session`. Herdr reads this value from your config and never adds or rewrites it.
+
 ## Agent session restore
 
 Herdr resumes supported Agent conversations after a server restart by default:
